# 0306 = 0305 plus two independent config-time switches (one build).
#
# A (default ON): write U3D_USB2_EPCTL_LPM_FC_CHK (0x0860) = 0x00060000 at
#   endpoint config.  Vendor TWRP stable frame has 0x00060000 (EP1/EP2 RX
#   L1 FC check); our hardware default 0x00fe00ff also sets EP0/TX checks.
#   Switch: ruby_lpmfcp=0 disables A.
# B (default OFF): skip the config-time TX state_reset (stop + FLUSHFIFO +
#   ring reset) that vendor mtu3_ep_enable does not perform.
#   Switch: ruby_cfgnoflush=1 enables B.
# Banner gate: "RUBY USB: 0306 lpmfcp=%d cfgnoflush=%d".
#
# Rationale (docs/122 §4b): the clean immediate write->read still fails
# after CL-0305; the only static vendor diff at the stable idle frame is
# 0x860.  Runtime EP0 w32 of the vendor value did not change the first read,
# so the write must happen at config (A).  B is the fallback axis.
#
# Arms: default (A) -> clean immediate-read; ruby_cfgnoflush=1 (A+B) if
# residual.  Baseline cmdline: config/0306-boot.cmdline (544 B, txreset=0).
# patchset: 272f54217e96259714aec77541febc3320f048a040e433125110b4c0af6ef30d
#           (289 files, computed locally from baseline-mirror)
